  :adr/decision
  "1. This iteration's single ranked move: start core-banking-prod at the gap register, not at code. Before any productionization edit on open-banking, it must be possible to query what still blocks production.
2. The register is proposed as datoms: a prod-readiness gate set on open-banking with one measured gate per entry - deploy surface (worker/wrangler.jsonc 404-check vs origin), D1 schema/migrations presence, xrpc-adapter routing coverage, form -> banking.ts wiring, Open Banking contract test (kotoba/test/banking.test.ts), and a transact-plane probe flag recording the owner-only measurement date. Each gate carries :prod/status open|closed|pending-owner with :prod/measure date and :prod/evidence source string, DataScript-queryable.
3. This ADR only registers the gap and the datom shape (propose-only). The register file lands in a following iteration only if owner accepts; the bot does not touch open-banking source yet, does not deploy, does not enter credentials, and does not modify kessai :redirect."
  :adr/consequences
  "Future kinyu ticks compare diffs against the register: each open gate is a ranked candidate and each tick proposes exactly one gate implementation PR, measured. The bot stays propose-only and never actuates payments: transfer/card execution, publishing and governor-bypass remain out of scope. Owner review of this ADR accepts or rejects the register shape before any repository edit takes place."
  :adr/gaps
  "1. Transact plane (401/502 on 2026-09-05) is owner-only to re-measure; health-200 is not a transact proof.
2. open-banking has no 90-docs dir yet. Register datoms are proposed for the corpus root, mirroring the workspace convention (90-docs/adr, DataScript queries).
3. app-open-swift relay DNS and NSID 6 legs remain design-only (unverified); ranked below this gap.
4. No production datoms exist on any of the 9 corpora; this ADR is the first."
